{"body":"Original finitely presented counterexample question remains unsolved after five substantive turns. This draft preserves all36 frozen author files and five manifest-bound independent-review files, plus a portable replay and reading guide.\n\nScoped results: bounded derived subgroup for every finitely generated metabelian group with explicit d(d+1) word bound; virtually metabelian exclusion; preservation of either dichotomy under finitely generated split abelian extensions; exact rational stable-norm computation on a supplied bounded-derived class; and a finite braid-shift repair obstruction. The LP does not recognize its input hypothesis. Ordinary homogeneous quasimorphisms are distinguished from partial ones. The finite braid detector and infinite-shift displacement bound are credited primary inputs.\n\nFull independent scoped PASS:345,888 author assertions and47,964 separate controls. No novelty or external peer-review certification, no finite-presentation counterexample or general theorem claimed.\n\nFresh main is first parent, frozen WIP second parent. Only target artifacts and own QUEUE status/turn cells changed to unsolved5/5. Standard-library Python replay passes; public source count0 explicitly omits raw PDF/screenshot hashes. No raw imports/private working audit, merge or release.","headRefOid":"420ffdfbb021c5a9378ccbbac198a13a4508dfad","isDraft":true,"mergeCommit":null,"mergeStateStatus":"UNKNOWN","mergeable":"UNKNOWN","mergedAt":null,"state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/380"}
